design:A-lists.schemaSql:
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------ Stream A: lists, asset context, requests and dashboard
-- A requester may withdraw their own request before it becomes or joins a work order. mt_requests' status CHECK (0018) is
-- not changed: a withdrawn request is 'closed', and these two columns say it was withdrawn, when and why (the person is
-- requested_by, who alone may withdraw it).
ALTER TABLE mt_requests ADD COLUMN withdrawn_at INTEGER;
ALTER TABLE mt_requests ADD COLUMN withdraw_reason TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
-- The work order list's date filters (raised, completed, due start) and its due-start sort.
CREATE INDEX mt_work_orders_created ON mt_work_orders(company_id, created_at);
CREATE INDEX mt_work_orders_due_start ON mt_work_orders(company_id, status, due_start);
CREATE INDEX mt_work_orders_completed ON mt_work_orders(company_id, completed_at) WHERE completed_at IS NOT NULL;
-- Note: 0018's comment on mt_wo_parts ("issuing from stores is a later stage") is out of date. Parts are issued from the
-- maintenance stores through ERP Inventory since stages M2 and M3 (mt_wo_stock, 0024). 0018 is not edited.

design:A-lists.reverseSql:
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS mt_work_orders_completed;
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS mt_work_orders_due_start;
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS mt_work_orders_created;
ALTER TABLE mt_requests DROP COLUMN withdraw_reason;
ALTER TABLE mt_requests DROP COLUMN withdrawn_at;
-- Withdrawn requests stay status 'closed' (a valid 0018 status) and keep their 'Withdrawn: <reason>' comment and request.withdrawn history line; nothing else to undo.

clientFiles.change:
WorkOrdersPage (lines 37-158):
- View = 'mine' | 'outstanding' | 'today' | 'week' | 'overdue' | 'unassigned' | 'all'. Tabs: My work (hidden for requesters), Outstanding, Due today, Due this week, Overdue, Unassigned (managers only), All. A requester opening ?view=mine or ?view=unassigned falls back to outstanding.
- Query: today, tzOffset = new Date().getTimezoneOffset(), limit 100, offset from the address. mine, outstanding, today, week and unassigned send status = g('status') || 'outstanding'. today and week add due=today|week; mine adds mine=1; unassigned adds unassigned=1. overdue sends status=overdue. all sends g('status').
- Filter keys copied from the address: priority, jobType, trade, assetId, includeChildren, siteId, assignedTo, raisedBy, departmentId, department, contractor, raisedFrom, raisedTo, dueStartFrom, dueStartTo, dueFrom, dueTo, completedFrom, completedTo, q, sort, dir.
- set() also deletes 'offset' whenever another key changes.
- The trade select moves out of the FilterPanel into the tabs row ('All trades' plus list.data.trades), so it stays visible on phones.
- FilterPanel fields:
  - Search, Status, Priority, Job type;
  - Raised from/to, Due start from/to, Due finish from/to, Completed from/to (type=date);
  - Department (DepartmentField pattern: a select of me.departments, or a text input with no departments);
  - Raised by (PersonSelect of me.people with empty 'Anyone');
  - Technician (assignedTo, PersonSelect minRole technician, managers only);
  - Contractor (text); Site (select from useSites);
  - Asset with 'Include child assets'; Sort by; Order;
  - a 'Clear filters' button (keeps view) when any are active.
- SORTS labels: { due: 'Due finish', dueStart: 'Due start', created: 'Date raised', finish: 'Completed', number: 'Number', priority: 'Priority', asset: 'Asset number', jobType: 'Job type', status: 'Status' }.
- A CSV link in the tabs row: <a className="btn" href={appUrl(`/api${mtPath(companyId, `/work-orders?${csvQuery}`)}`)} download><Icon name="download" /> CSV</a>. csvQuery is the query without limit and offset, plus format=csv.
- A pager row under the table: 'Showing 101 to 200 of 340' with Previous and Next buttons that set offset. When total > 5000, a muted note says 'The CSV has the first 5,000.'
- Empty states: 'Nothing is due today.', 'Nothing else is due this week.', 'Every open work order has a technician.'
NewWorkOrderPage line 252: 'Write each part and the quantity the job needs. Parts taken from the maintenance stores are recorded on the work order under Parts used.' If the parts stream (MX-06) rewrites that section, its text wins.
WorkOrderDetail: insert <AssetPanel companyId={companyId} assetId={w.assetId} excludeWorkOrderId={w.id} /> right after the Details Section (after line 417), and delete the otherOutstandingOnAsset paragraph (line 416). The panel shows the same figure. The server field stays.

